WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.530
With Amazon Global Selling, you can expand your business and reach customers across the globe by

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:13.700
listing your products in Amazon stores worldwide.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:20.220
Use the "sell globally" experience to discover your top countries and Amazon stores for expansion.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:26.751
Determine your costs of selling in these new stores and receive expert guidance and resources to

00:00:26.751 --> 00:00:27.520
launch successfully.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:34.217
Access "sell globally" by navigating to the main seller central menu, hovering over the inventory

00:00:34.217 --> 00:00:36.640
tab and clicking on "sell globally".

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:43.469
The new stores to launch section uses two different views to help you explore your potential in

00:00:43.469 --> 00:00:44.200
additional stores.

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:50.138
Region view compares your opportunity across different regions, including potential sales, any incentives

00:00:50.138 --> 00:00:52.611
Amazon provides to support your launch,

00:00:52.611 --> 00:00:59.280
and an estimate of the year one investment you would make to expand to your highest potential store.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:04.300
Store view shows similar data, plus recommended ASINs in a table view.

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:09.700
This view is especially useful if you have multiple stores to consider expanding into.

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:16.480
The next section, "Global Sales in Active Stores" lets you view a summary of your sales performance

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:17.840
in your current stores,

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:20.400
plus an estimate of your sales opportunity when available.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:27.617
Stores will only appear in the "Global Sales in Active Stores" section if you already have an account

00:01:27.617 --> 00:01:28.820
in that store.

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:33.734
If you have an account in another store that is not showing up in "Global Sales in Active Stores",

00:01:33.734 --> 00:01:36.320
you may need to link it to your other accounts.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:42.800
Scroll down to "Amazon Stores Worldwide" and click "Link Account" next to that store.

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:48.416
And when you're ready to expand to a new store listed in the "Amazon Stores Worldwide" table, simply

00:01:48.416 --> 00:01:50.600
click "Register" next to the new store.

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:55.640
You can access powerful data about your expansion opportunities on the expansion research page,

00:01:55.640 --> 00:02:02.480
which you can get to from the new stores to launch section by clicking on "View Details in Region

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:04.640
View" or "Details in Store View".

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:11.270
You can also get to the expansion research page from the "Global Sales in Active Stores" section

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:14.780
by clicking on a sales opportunity amount if available.

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:20.870
When you're on the expansion research page, select a region from the drop-down and then select a

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:23.020
specific store to see relevant data.

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:28.460
You'll see a summary of the opportunity in that store, including your estimated first-year sales

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:34.580
and the cost to launch in that store based on the top ASINs which are displayed as well.

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:40.925
Under the "Summary", the "Sales Insights" tab shows category trends and predicted demand for your

00:02:40.925 --> 00:02:43.020
catalog in the target store.

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:50.364
Sales projection by category is the first chart shown and you can filter the data by your current

00:02:50.364 --> 00:02:56.484
catalog's categories or brands and can compare between gross merchandise sales or GMS and number

00:02:56.484 --> 00:02:57.300
of units.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:03.600
Beneath this chart, you will see six graphs, which you can filter by category and time frame.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:11.465
These charts show category sales trend, top ASINs sales, sales across price bands, return ratio,

00:03:11.465 --> 00:03:15.660
advertising cost of sales and Amazon fees comparison.

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:22.325
For some target stores, you will also see the "Cost Analysis" tab, which shows an estimate of the

00:03:22.325 --> 00:03:28.619
variable and one-time costs of your first year, assuming you launch your top 10 recommended ASINs

00:03:28.619 --> 00:03:30.100
in the target store.

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:35.220
These costs are estimates only and final costs depend on various factors.

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:41.887
The estimated sales, incentive to launch if applicable, variable costs and one-time costs are outlined

00:03:41.887 --> 00:03:45.220
in the "Cost Breakdown" table on the left.

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:49.460
Click on the drop-down arrow for each estimate to see more details.

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:56.308
On the right, Amazon will provide estimated shipping costs and estimates for additional ASIN specific

00:03:56.308 --> 00:03:59.960
costs if these estimates are applicable and available.

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:06.200
Use the links in this section to explore additional programs and find trusted service providers

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:08.280
to support your expansion journey.

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:14.479
When you're ready to expand to the target store, simply click "Sign Up" at the top of the Expansion

00:04:14.479 --> 00:04:18.720
Research page to be taken to the Account Registration page for that store.
